Notable judgment calls: unit 3's window has S2-complete fused with S3's opening fragment ("...by Go. In addition,") on every candidate that otherwise looks close (e.g. c04) — none isolate "In addition, that tool got..." on its own line, so I flagged it missing. Unit 5's 472-char line has 4 sentences; every candidate leaves at least two of them sharing a line (usually S1+S2), so none pass — my version keeps S2/S3 whole (no internal boundary, borderline/no-boundary long lines left alone) but splits S4 at "that" (a genuine relative-pronoun boundary, and S4 alone runs ~134 chars).
